From: EasyStick maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] host: defer Bluetooth initialization in Wi-Fi-only lab

The AddOn C6 advertises WLAN and BLE over SDIO.  The M3 lab acceptance scope
is WLAN plus SSH.  Keep ESP-Hosted's Bluetooth code linked (the upstream
module shares helper symbols), but deliberately do not create an HCI device.
That prevents an optional BLE setup timeout from racing the WLAN association
test.  A later Bluetooth milestone must replace this guard with its own
tested initialization path.

---
 main.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -235,4 +235,8 @@ static void init_bt(struct esp_adapter *adapter)
 {
 
+	if ((adapter->capabilities & ESP_BT_SPI_SUPPORT) ||
+		(adapter->capabilities & ESP_BT_SDIO_SUPPORT))
+		return;
+
 	if ((adapter->capabilities & ESP_BT_SPI_SUPPORT) ||
 		(adapter->capabilities & ESP_BT_SDIO_SUPPORT)) {
-- 
